-
-## Prepare execution and closeout
-
-Before every staged dispatch, follow the dispatch-preparation section of
-`workspace-control/docs/multica-workflow.md`: populate `trackself_dispatch`,
-resolve baseline refs from the owning manifest, and validate the selected
-runtime against the stage's capabilities. This check belongs before assignment,
-not inside an evaluator already known to lack its required environment.
-
-Persist results and criteria in the issue body and read them back. Optional
-comments are not closeout gates. Use the authorized terminal child transition
-as the single parent wake; never manufacture comment IDs or another launch to
-compensate for unavailable communication. Classify recovery using task-context.md.
-
-## Treat the compact projection as structural authority
-
-Retrieve the complete parent once. Then run:
-
-```sh
-workspace-control/scripts/trackself-multica-context <parent>
-```
-
-On a stage wake, also pass `--trigger-child <child>`.
-
-A stable `compact_full_audit` projection is the complete structural authority
-for the collected topology and task history. Do not repeat its raw native reads
-in model context. In particular, do not run `multica issue children`, enumerate
-all child runs, retrieve every child, or scan all parent comments or metadata
-after a stable projection.
-
