-- every record named by `detail_required`;
-- relevant actual-workspace evidence;
-- the smallest plausible matching or conflicting child set needed for a
-  semantic matching or supersession decision; and
-- exact mutation targets for their required read-backs.
-
-An `unstable` or `error` projection permits no mutation. Retry the read-only
-collection or perform the documented complete manual fallback. Manual fallback
-is recovery, not the ordinary path.
-
-## Reconcile before creating or dispatching
-
-Adopt a matching pre-created child. Reconcile duplicate, stale, superseded, or
-conflicting children before dispatch. Escalate ambiguous ownership or
-supersession to the Primary.
-
-Verify that the lowest unfinished stage contains exactly its intended children
-and that every future-stage child is unassigned in `backlog`. Do not pre-assign
-parked children. When the approved parent explicitly permits independent
-parallel children, the stage barrier closes only after every child in that
-stage is terminal; otherwise dispatch one current child at a time.
-
