-stage, cancellation, or failure transition is material to the decision.
-
-## Enforce the managed-repository Forgejo baton
-
-For a lane whose declared execution target is `managed_repositories`, normal
-cross-role continuity is a Forgejo feature branch and one issue-linked pull
-request. Lane enrollment supplies the narrow authority to commit and normally
-push the task branch and to create or update that PR. Author every Implementor
-child to finish only after recording the PR URL, source branch, and verified
-exact remote head. Author the Review Controller child against that head and
-require routine fixes to be committed and fast-forward pushed to the same PR.
-Author each Acceptance Reviewer child to inspect the exact live remote head
-read-only.
-
-Do not invent a second publication approval, add a no-push boundary, or use a
-retained sibling task checkout as ordinary source transport. Retained worktrees
-may support reconciliation or an explicitly authorized recovery only. A parent
-that forbids remote feature-branch or PR publication is incompatible with the
-managed lane. Force push, merge, PR closure, default-branch mutation, tagging,
-release, artifact publication, and deployment remain outside this transport
-authority.
-
-## Reconcile a done child before its wake
-
-Before an authorized specialist marks its child `done`, it updates every
-existing checkbox that describes the child's own deliverable and the
-current-state section against recorded evidence, states any remaining action or
-that none remains, persists and reads the description back, then posts its
-result, marks the child `done`, and reads the complete child back. Acceptance-verdict
-checkboxes describe evaluation and verdict delivery; product acceptance
-predicates are non-checkbox inputs so any valid verdict can complete the child.
