-
-`trackself-multica-project-workspace check-issue <child> --environment <key>`
-checks these requirements before dispatch. Assignment, rerun, starting status
-or body updates, and role-bound replies enforce the same requirements. Create
-children unassigned first. Terminal transitions deliberately do not require
-capabilities, dependencies, or a comment thread: they must remain available to
-report an evaluation that could not run. Task-free recordkeeping remains possible.
-
-Capabilities are conservative routing declarations in
-`config/multica-project-workspace.toml`, not proof of a live session. No current
-lane declares `kde-x11`, authenticated QA fixtures, or an interactive GUI. A stage
-requiring one must declare it, and cannot be dispatched until a suitable target
-is verified and declared. Do not erase requirements to pass the guard. Actual
-session, fixture, credentials and candidate evidence must still be checked at
-that target; never put secrets in metadata. Empty lists/maps are valid only when
-the stage needs no special capability/repository baseline. Parent intake remains
-possible without metadata; staged children must have it, including old children
-before a new dispatch after rollout.
-
-The issue body is the required result channel. Store the outcome, criteria and
-evidence, read it back, then perform and read back the authorized terminal
-transition exactly once. Existing-thread comments are optional communication;
-missing threads or comment failure cannot block closeout. Keep reply guards
-strict and do not fabricate parent IDs. The provider's child-terminal event is
-the only automatic parent wake. A lost response requires state reconciliation,
-not a second assignment or comment trigger.
-
-For recovery, distinguish a code defect (fix plus affected checks), unavailable
-evaluation prerequisites (resume the stage on the unchanged candidate), and
-communication failure (reconcile delivery only). Preserve independent acceptance
-and fresh verdict identity; a verdict already completed is not an interrupted
-evaluation. Record escalation owner, exact unresolved question, evidence, next
-safe action and delivery acknowledgement. No acknowledgement means delivery is
-unproven, not that the user rejected or must rediscover the work.
-
-Rollout requires these scripts, the schema-7 environment declaration, and role
-instructions together. Prepare pending children before redispatch; do not rerun
-completed engineering stages just to add metadata. Read-only unit/integration
-checks are not live Multica exactly-once proof. Live role application and runtime
-checkout updates follow the separately scoped deployment authority.
